":559,"data":{"type":"EssentialElements\\FrequentlyAskedQuestions","properties":{"content":{"settings":{"questions":[{"question":"Is recovery really possible?","answer":"We wish to assure you that there is a solution and that recovery is possible. It begins with complete abstinence from cocaine and all other mind-altering substances and continues with practising C.A.’s Twelve Steps of recovery one day at a time."},{"question":"Does it cost anything to attend C.A.?","answer":"C.A. is free. Each C.A. group is fully self-supporting. Expenses are covered by the voluntary contributions of members, literature sales and fundraising events such as conventions. C.A. respectfully declines donations and financial contributions from any outside source.","button":null},{"answer":"While the name “Cocaine Anonymous” may sound drug specific, we wish to assure you that our program is not. It doesn’t matter to us if you drank or what type of drugs you used; if you have a desire to stop you are welcome here.","question":"Is Cocaine Anonymous only for people who use cocaine?","button":{"text":"Click Here"}}],"accordion":false,"first_tab_open":false,"first_tab_opened":true,"items":[{"answer":"The essence of C.A. is the spiritual concept of one addict helping another. Sponsors act as mentors or guides, helping sponsees work through the Twelve Steps. We hold regular meetings to further this fellowship, allowing new members to find us and, perhaps, the answers they seek.","question":"What happens in a meeting?"},{"answer":"Our public relations policy is based on attraction rather than promotion - we need always maintain personal anonymity at the level of press, radio, television and films. Anonymity is the spiritual foundation of all our Traditions, ever reminding us to place principles before personalities.","question":"Will our privacy be protected?"},{"answer":"C.A. offers a twenty-five-question self-help test. If any answer is “yes”, there may be a problem. The pamphlet closes with clear direction: there is an answer - come to meetings of Cocaine Anonymous.","question":"How can we tell if our loved one needs help?","button":null},{"answer":"<p>Simply having a fellow addict and member of Cocaine Anonymous accompany the newcomer to a meeting can encourage them to stay. Our hope is to help overcome hesitations about attending, whether those include denial, inconvenience, fear or limited resources.</p>","question":"How do we encourage a first meeting?","button":null},{"question":"What is the solution C.A. uses?","answer":"Cocaine Anonymous practises a Twelve-Step program for daily recovery that has worked for many thousands worldwide. It is a program of action - sober addicts freely helping other addicts through sponsorship by taking them through the Twelve Steps of recovery."},{"question":"Is C.A. a religious organisation?","answer":"C.A. is spiritual but not religious, and members are free to define their spirituality as they see fit. Central to our program is an emphasis on a spiritual awakening and its practical value."}]}},"design":{"main_container":{"borders":{"border":null},"max_width":{"number":650,"unit":"px","style":"650px"}},"item_containers":{"spacing":{"padding":null},"borders":null},"icon":{"icon_animation":"rotation","icon":{"slug":"icon-chevron-right.","name":"chevron right","svgCode":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 512\"><!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.1 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --><path d=\"M285.476 272.971L91.132 467.314c-9.373 9.373-24.569 9.373-33.941 0l-22.667-22.667c-9.357-9.357-9.375-24.522-.04-33.901L188.505 256 34.484 101.255c-9.335-9.379-9.317-24.544.04-33.901l22.667-22.667c9.373-9.373 24.569-9.373 33.941 0L285.475 239.03c9.373 9.372 9.373 24.568.001 33.941z\"/></svg>"},"icon_rotation":{"number":90,"unit":"deg","style":"90deg"},"second_icon":{"slug":"icon-times.","name":"times","